.TH AVR\-VM\-LIST 1 "" "avr 0.6.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-vm-list \- List the organization's VMs, newest first (deleted ones excluded).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr vm list
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the organization's VMs, newest first (deleted ones excluded).
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Filter by lifecycle state. (choices: PENDING, STARTING, RUNNING, PAUSING, PAUSED, STOPPING, DELETING, FAILED)
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Visible VMs or only your own. (choices: all, mine; default: all)
.TP
\fB\-\-sandbox\fR / \fB\-\-no\-sandbox\fR
Agent sandboxes only, or human-created VMs only.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR, \fB\-\-limit\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
Max VMs to return. (default: 50)
.TP
\fB\-\-cursor\fR \fITEXT\fR
Pagination cursor from a previous response.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the VM list as JSON.
